Arrays vs. Linked List

ArrayList requires moving element to insert a new element
	This can be a lengthy process on a large list

Linked lists use pointer to point to the address of the next element

Linked List has each element and a pointer to the next element
	This is faster to add or remove items, as you just update the value of the pointer (the value pointing to the next element)
	Linked lists require more memory and can take longer to search






